.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2416:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/003-build-benchmark-mode/spec.md:126:| REQ-002 | Mode switch works end-to-end | `loop-host.cjs --mode=model-benchmark` materializes fixtures → runs benchmark → writes a `benchmark_run` record → `promote-candidate.cjs --mode=model-benchmark` returns a decision |
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2417:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/003-build-benchmark-mode/spec.md:127:| REQ-003 | Generic dispatcher | `dispatch-model.cjs` dispatches via executor-routing map; forwards `--variant` only for model-benchmark; never loaded in agent-improvement mode |
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2418:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/003-build-benchmark-mode/spec.md:133:| REQ-004 | Scorer decoupled from fixture JSON | Scorer reads primitive criteria arrays (not raw fixture files); det-checks are cwd-decoupled — the scorer synthesizes a virtual fixture with an ABSOLUTE `scope.cwd`, and det-checks resolve `path.resolve(PACKET_ROOT, scope.cwd)` (a no-op for an absolute path), so no packet-relative coupling remains (122 review F-P2-3: this supersedes the earlier "det-checks accept explicit `--cwd`" wording — the decoupling is achieved via the absolute virtual-fixture cwd, not a literal flag); `buildGraderFn(mode)` factory in place |
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2419:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/003-build-benchmark-mode/spec.md:143:- **SC-002**: A real `--mode=model-benchmark` run produces a scored `benchmark_run` record and a promotion decision, with every record carrying the correct `mode`.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2420:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/003-build-benchmark-mode/spec.md:153:| Risk | Modifying live deep-agent-improvement scripts regresses agent-improvement | High | TST-1 byte-identity gate + run the existing vitest suite before/after every change |
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2421:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/003-build-benchmark-mode/spec.md:154:| Risk | Scorer fixture-coupling decoupling is the hardest part (3 coupling points + det-check scripts) | Med | Land the additive new files first; decouple incrementally with the scorer's own tests |
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2422:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/003-build-benchmark-mode/spec.md:156:| Risk | promote-candidate already branches on benchmark-complete (partial mode-awareness) | Low | Extend the existing branch rather than bolt on `--mode` from scratch |
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2423:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/003-build-benchmark-mode/spec.md:164:- RESOLVED: Copied/ported the scorer + det-checks + grader + cache into `scripts/scorer/` (no cross-packet runtime coupling). Runtime `scorer/cache/` is git-ignored.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2424:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/003-build-benchmark-mode/spec.md:165:- RESOLVED: `promote-candidate.cjs` routes by the score file's `status` (`scored` vs `benchmark-complete`) — already mode-aware, so no `--mode` flag was bolted on.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2425:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/003-build-benchmark-mode/spec.md:166:- Follow-on (P2): `score-model-variant.cjs` is available behind the scorer seam but `run-benchmark.cjs` still uses its pattern matcher by default; adopting the 5-dim scorer as the active model-benchmark scorer is a separate opt-in.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2426:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/003-build-benchmark-mode/spec.md:167:- ACCEPTED DEFERRAL (122 review F-P2-1/F-P2-2, Opus-4.8-arbitrated): the model-benchmark default path intentionally scores pre-materialized outputs via the pattern matcher and does NOT invoke `dispatch-model.cjs` or `score-model-variant.cjs`. REQ-003/REQ-004 require those seams to be decoupled + available (satisfied), not wired as the default. Phase 004 deliberately did NOT force-wire them — a half-baked opt-in (run-benchmark fixtures carry headings/patterns, not the acceptance/grading criteria the 5-dim scorer needs) would be lower quality than the clean documented deferral. Wire when a benchmark genuinely needs fresh model generation + 5-dim rubric scoring.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2427:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:3:description: "Architecture decisions for moving the deep-agent-improvement scripts into lane subdirs: lane classification, TST-1-preserving spawn-time lane resolution, the dispatch-model silent-config-failure trap, and keeping lib and tests at the scripts root."
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2428:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:7:  - "deep-agent-improvement scripts decision record"
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2429:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:12:    packet_pointer: "skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg"
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2430:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:19:      - ".opencode/skills/deep-agent-improvement/scripts/loop-host.cjs"
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2431:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:20:      - ".opencode/skills/deep-agent-improvement/scripts/dispatch-model.cjs"
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2432:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:37:## ADR-001: Lane Classification of the 16 Scripts
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2433:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:52:Phases 010-012 split references, assets, the agent note, the catalog, and the advisor by lane, but the 16 scripts plus the scorer subtree are still flat at `scripts/`. We need a classification that puts each script under the lane it actually serves, so the tree mirrors the two co-equal lanes.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2434:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:55:- Classification must reflect runtime ownership, not just naming: a script that loop-host spawns on the model-benchmark path may still be shared if both lanes use it.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2435:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:56:- The scorer subtree must move wholesale into model-benchmark so its internal relative requires (`./harness.cjs`, `../lib/cache.cjs`) stay valid.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2436:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:64:**We chose**: Three lane subdirs - agent-improvement (8 scripts), model-benchmark (2 scripts + scorer/), shared (6 scripts).
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2437:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:66:**How it works**: agent-improvement holds score-candidate, generate-profile, rollback-candidate, candidate-lineage, scan-integration, check-mirror-drift, trade-off-detector, benchmark-stability. model-benchmark holds dispatch-model, run-benchmark, and the scorer/ subtree moved as one unit. shared holds loop-host, promote-candidate, materialize-benchmark-fixtures, reduce-state, improvement-journal, mutation-coverage - scripts both lanes invoke or that orchestrate across lanes.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2438:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:77:| Two lanes only, shared folded into agent-improvement | Fewer dirs | loop-host and materialize would be mislabeled as agent-only | 5/10 |
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2439:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:80:**Why this one**: A dedicated shared lane is the only honest home for loop-host (which orchestrates both modes) and materialize-benchmark-fixtures (which loop-host spawns on the benchmark path but is fixture infra). It also matches the references/assets layout shipped in 010.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2440:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:99:| materialize misclassified | M | shared is correct: it is fixture infra loop-host spawns, not benchmark-only logic |
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2441:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:100:| scorer relative requires break | M | move scorer/ wholesale so internal requires stay valid |
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2442:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:112:| 3 | **Sufficient?** | PASS | Three subdirs cover all 16 scripts plus scorer |
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2443:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:113:| 4 | **Fits Goal?** | PASS | On the critical path to a fully lane-visible skill |
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2444:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:125:- `scripts/agent-improvement/`, `scripts/model-benchmark/`, `scripts/shared/` created via git mv.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2445:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:126:- scorer/ moved into model-benchmark/scorer/ as one unit.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2446:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:135:## ADR-002: TST-1-Preserving Lane Resolution at Spawn Time
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2447:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:149:`loop-host.cjs` is moving to the shared lane, but it spawns children across all three lanes: score-candidate (agent-improvement), materialize-benchmark-fixtures (shared), and run-benchmark (model-benchmark). Its `planInvocation(mode, args)` is a pure planner that returns ordered steps with bare script names, and the TST-1 backward-compat test asserts the default and explicit agent-improvement plans are byte-identical. If lane paths leak into the plan, that identity breaks.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2448:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:161:**How it works**: `planInvocation` continues to emit `{ script: 'score-candidate.cjs', args }` style steps with bare names. A new lane-resolution map in the spawn layer translates each bare name to its `scripts/<lane>/<name>` path right before `spawnSync`. The plan stays byte-identical; only execution knows about lanes.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2449:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:171:| Keep all loop-host children in one lane | No spawn-layer change | Forces a wrong lane on at least two children | 3/10 |
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2450:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:181:- Lane knowledge is isolated to the execution boundary.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2451:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:191:| A child spawned at wrong path | H | non-zero exit surfaces loudly; loop-host aborts remaining steps |
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2452:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:199:| 1 | **Necessary?** | PASS | loop-host spawns across all three lanes |
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2453:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:212:- `loop-host.cjs` runNode/runPlan gain a bare-name to lane-path resolver.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2454:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:215:**How to roll back**: Revert the resolver edit and move loop-host back to the scripts root; the bare `path.join(SCRIPTS_ROOT, name)` then works again at the flat layout.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2455:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:221:## ADR-003: Guarding the dispatch-model Silent-Config-Failure Trap
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2456:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:235:`dispatch-model.cjs` sets `SCRIPTS_ROOT = __dirname` and then resolves `path.join(SCRIPTS_ROOT, '..', 'state')` and `path.join(SCRIPTS_ROOT, '..', 'assets', 'agent-improvement', 'improvement_config.json')`. At the flat layout `..` is the skill root. After moving into `scripts/model-benchmark/`, `..` becomes the scripts root, so both paths miss. `loadConfig` wraps the read in try/catch and returns `{}` on any failure, so a wrong depth produces no error: dispatch silently runs with default model, agent, timeout, and backoff while the journal and dashboard claim the configured values.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2457:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:247:**How it works**: After moving into `scripts/model-benchmark/`, the state and assets joins gain one more `..` (or resolve from a computed skill-root anchor) so they point at the skill root again. A regression test materializes a known `improvement_config.json` and asserts dispatch-model reads the expected `modelBenchmarkConfig` values, catching any future silent fallback to `{}`.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2458:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:288:| 4 | **Fits Goal?** | PASS | protects the model-benchmark lane the move touches |
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2459:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:298:- `dispatch-model.cjs` state and assets path joins gain the correct depth.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2460:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:301:**How to roll back**: Revert the depth edit and move dispatch-model back to the scripts root, where the original `..` depth is correct.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2461:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/016-script-subfolder-readmes/description.json:2:  "specFolder": "121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/016-script-subfolder-readmes",
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2462:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/016-script-subfolder-readmes/description.json:3:  "description": "Add sk-doc-aligned code-folder READMEs to every source script subfolder under deep-agent-improvement/scripts and audit the 3 existing READMEs.",
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2463:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/016-script-subfolder-readmes/description.json:7:    "deep-agent-improvement scripts",
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2464:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/016-script-subfolder-readmes/description.json:11:    "model-benchmark",
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2465:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/016-script-subfolder-readmes/description.json:18:    "121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode"
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2466:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/deep-research-config.json:2:  "topic": "How should we implement the deep-agent-improvement model-benchmark mode designed in 001? Define exact interface contracts for the three pluggable seams (candidate-source, dispatcher, scorer); how to generalize the 120/003 dispatch-minimax.cjs into a model-agnostic dispatch-model.cjs; how to port the 120/003 eval-rig scorer + 5-dim rubric cleanly into deep-agent-improvement; how to wire a mode switch (agent-improvement | model-benchmark) into loop.cjs without regressing the agent-improvement path; the backward-compat test strategy; and implementation edge cases/pitfalls. Output build-ready guidance: per-seam interface contracts plus a wiring + backward-compat plan as a build-delta list.",
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2467:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/deep-research-config.json:10:  "specFolder": ".opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research",
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2468:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/deep-research-config.json:20:    "model": "minimax/MiniMax-M2.7",
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2469:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/prompts/iteration-4.md:11:Questions: 3/5 answered | Last focus: Q3: Port the 120/003 eval-rig scorer and 5-dim rubric — decouple deterministic checks + claude grader harness from fixture-only assumptions
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2470:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/prompts/iteration-4.md:14:Next focus: Q4: Wire the mode switch into `loop.cjs` — implement the actual code changes including `reduce-state.cjs`, `converge.cjs`, and ensure `materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs` is only invoked for model-benchmark mode.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2471:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/prompts/iteration-4.md:16:Research Topic: How should we implement the deep-agent-improvement model-benchmark mode designed in 001? Define exact interface contracts for the three pluggable seams (candidate-source, dispatcher, scorer); generalize 120/003 dispatch-minimax.cjs into a model-agnostic dispatch-model.cjs; port the 120/003 eval-rig scorer + 5-dim rubric cleanly; wire a mode switch (agent-improvement | model-benchmark) into loop.cjs without regressing agent-improvement; backward-compat test strategy; implementation edge cases. Output per-seam interface contracts + a wiring/backward-compat build-delta list.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2472:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/prompts/iteration-4.md:18:Focus Area: Q4: Wire the mode switch into `loop.cjs` — implement the actual code changes including `reduce-state.cjs`, `converge.cjs`, and ensure `materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs` is only invoked for model-benchmark mode.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2473:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/prompts/iteration-4.md:19:Remaining Key Questions: - **Q4**: Wire mode switch into `loop.cjs`, `reduce-state.cjs`, `converge.cjs`, `materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs` — actual code changes
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2474:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/prompts/iteration-4.md:21:Last 3 Iterations Summary: run 1: Q1: Define exact interface contracts for the three pluggable (0.35); run 2: Q2: Design dispatch-model.cjs generalization — config schema (0.45); run 3: Q3: Port the 120/003 eval-rig scorer and 5-dim rubric — deco (0.55)
