.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2596:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/003-build-benchmark-mode/plan.md:30:# Implementation Plan: Phase 1: build-benchmark-mode
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2597:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:5:Implement the mode switch (agent-improvement | model-benchmark) wiring in `loop.cjs` (the orchestrating entry point) and ensure `materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs` is only invoked for model-benchmark mode. Research the actual code changes needed in reduce-state.cjs, converge.cjs, and the materialize plumbing.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2598:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:10:2. **Read `materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs`** — standalone fixture materializer, invoked independently of the agent-improvement loop.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2599:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:11:3. **Read `run-benchmark.cjs`** — the benchmark-mode scorer (fixture-based, pattern matching).
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2600:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:12:4. **Read `score-candidate.cjs`** — the agent-improvement scorer (5-dim rubric, profile-driven).
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2601:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:17:### F1 — deep-agent-improvement has no `loop.cjs` — the loop IS the orchestration
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2602:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:19:The deep-agent-improvement skill does not have a `loop.cjs`. Its "loop" is the journal-serialized orchestration via:
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2603:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:22:- `promote-candidate.cjs` — decides based on scores whether to accept/reject
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2604:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:24:The 120/003 `loop.cjs` is a synchronous imperative script that coordinates `dispatch → score → converge → mutate` in a single process. deep-agent-improvement uses a different pattern: async journal appends, separate reducer runs, and explicit promotion gating.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2605:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:26:**Implication**: The "mode switch" for deep-agent-improvement must be implemented at the **entry point** that drives the journal-based loop (likely an `index.cjs` or `main.cjs` that doesn't yet exist), NOT inside reduce-state.cjs which is purely reactive.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2606:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:30:### F2 — `materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs` is already standalone and gated
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2607:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:32:This script (97 LOC) takes `--profile` and `--outputs-dir` as required args. It does NOT check any mode flag — it simply materializes fixtures when invoked. It is invoked by the benchmark runner (`run-benchmark.cjs`) as part of the benchmark scoring pipeline.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2608:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:34:For model-benchmark mode, `materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs` must be called before `run-benchmark.cjs`. For agent-improvement mode, neither is called. The current calling pattern is:
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2609:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:37:run-benchmark.cjs --profile <x> --outputs-dir <y>
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2610:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:38:  └── internally calls materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs? NO — they are separate scripts
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2611:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:41:Actually, `run-benchmark.cjs` does NOT call `materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs`. It loads fixtures directly via `loadFixtures()` (lines 85–93). The materializer is a **separate step** that must be called before `run-benchmark.cjs` to produce the `.md` output files that `scoreFixture()` reads.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2612:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:43:**Gating rule**: materialize should ONLY run when mode=`model-benchmark`. In agent-improvement, the benchmark pipeline is not relevant.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2613:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:49:`reduce-state.cjs` (1146 LOC) reads `agent-improvement-state.jsonl` and emits `experiment-registry.json` + `agent-improvement-dashboard.md`. It has NO mode awareness. Every record in the state log carries a `type` field that allows it to be bucketed correctly regardless of whether the record came from agent-improvement or model-benchmark scoring.
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2614:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:52:- `scored` / `accepted` / `rejected` — from score-candidate.cjs (agent-improvement)
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2615:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:53:- `benchmark_run` — from run-benchmark.cjs (model-benchmark)
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2616:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:54:- `infra_failure` — from either scorer
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2617:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:61:### F4 — converge.cjs is absent from deep-agent-improvement — it may be promote-candidate.cjs
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2618:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:63:No `converge.cjs` exists in `.opencode/skills/deep-agent-improvement/scripts/`. The convergence logic for agent-improvement is in `promote-candidate.cjs` which evaluates promotion gates (weighted score threshold, benchmark pass, stability coefficient). For model-benchmark mode, convergence is the `benchmark_run` record's `recommendation` field (`benchmark-pass` vs `benchmark-fail`).
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2619:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:65:The "converge" step in 120/003 evaluates whether a variant is the best seen so far. In deep-agent-improvement, this is done by:
.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2620:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/002-implementation-deep-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:66:- `promote-candidate.cjs` — computes `recommendation` from score + gates
