-.opencode/specs/system-spec-kit/026-graph-and-context-optimization/002-spec-kit-internals/002-skill-advisor/006-playbook-run-and-remediation/005-finding-remediation/007-harness-alias-and-stale-path/implementation-summary.md:52:Both regression harnesses now compare gold labels alias-aware, so a renamed skill (the live `deep-*` ids) satisfies a fixture labelled with its old `sk-deep-*` alias. The alias groups were the real gap: the Python groups lacked the `sk-deep-*` entries and neither language had a `deep-agent-improvement` group, so the matcher had nothing to resolve against. Completing the groups plus switching the harness compares to the existing alias helpers (`skill_matches_alias` in Python, `skillInAliasSet` in TS) clears the deep-* alias failures without editing the ground-truth fixtures.
