+| Toolformer | tool/API call annotation and usefulness filtering | [deepseek/iter2] [SOURCE: https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.04761] |
+| Self-RAG / RAGAS | adaptive retrieval, context precision/recall/utilization | [deepseek/iter1] [gpt55/iter1] [SOURCE: https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.11511] [SOURCE: https://docs.ragas.io/en/v0.1.21/concepts/metrics/index.html] |
+| LangSmith eval concepts | trace/trajectory and pairwise/reference evaluators | [gpt55/iter1] [SOURCE: https://docs.langchain.com/langsmith/evaluation-concepts?mode=ui] |
+| OpenAI evals / tracing / OpenTelemetry | schema-backed eval records and span/event traces | [gpt55/iter2] [SOURCE: https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/evals] [SOURCE: https://openai.github.io/openai-agents-python/tracing/] [SOURCE: https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otel/trace/api/] |
+| Large Language Monkeys | repeated-sampling coverage, useful for skill-on/off success delta | [minimax/iter1] [root/iter1] [SOURCE: arxiv.org/abs/2407.21787] |
+| MetaTool / MCP-Bench / AgentBench | tool-use awareness, similar-tool selection, fuzzy instructions, trajectory scoring | [gpt55/iter1] [opus/iter1] [SOURCE: https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.03128] [SOURCE: https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.20453] [SOURCE: https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.03688] |
+| MT-Bench / G-Eval / LLM-as-judge | semantic quality deltas for D4, with bias controls | [deepseek/iter1] [opus/iter1] [SOURCE: https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.05685] [SOURCE: https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.16634] |
 
-Since OpenCode exposes MCP tools natively, the tool-call trace can be captured at the MCP transport layer. This is the same approach the system-spec-kit's own `session_bootstrap` and `session_resume` use to track tool calls — the serialized transport records every `tool_use` block with its arguments. For Lane C, this means:
+Divergences:
 
-- Run the scenario via the OpenCode runtime directly (not through a CLI binary)
-- Capture the full session's tool-call log from the runtime's internal trace buffer
-- Filter to Read/Glob/Bash calls targeting files under `.opencode/skills/<target-skill>/`
+DeepSeek had the strongest verified external-source pass for BFCL, ToolBench, Self-RAG, Toolformer, and APE-style prompt generation [deepseek/iter1] [deepseek/iter2]. GPT-5.5 emphasized operational eval/tracing frameworks such as LangSmith, OpenAI evals, and OpenTelemetry [gpt55/iter1] [gpt55/iter2]. Opus gave useful prior-art mappings but flagged several external citations as `[web-unverified]` because web access was denied in its background context [opus/iter1] [opus/iter2].
 
-This approach is the highest fidelity but couples the harness to the OpenCode runtime. **Recommendation: Layer approaches — use Approach 1 (CLI output parse) as the default, with Approach 3 as an opt-in high-fidelity mode for skills where fine-grained trace analysis matters.**
+## 3. Recommended Lane C Design
 
-### RQ2-B: Holding Out the Expected-Resource Key
+### Scoring Model
 
-The expected-resource key is derived from the skill's own metadata. For each scenario, the key is:
+Composite score:
 
-```
-scenario_key = {
-  skill_slug: "deep-agent-improvement",
-  expected_intent: "MODEL_BENCHMARK",              // from INTENT_SIGNALS classification
-  expected_resources: [                             // from RESOURCE_MAP[MODEL_BENCHMARK]
-    "references/model-benchmark/benchmark_operator_guide.md",
-    "references/model-benchmark/evaluator_contract.md",
-  ],
-  expected_runtime_assets: [                        // from RUNTIME_ASSETS
-    "assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/default.json",
-  ],
-  always_resources: [                               // from RUNTIME_ASSETS["ALWAYS"]
-    "assets/agent-improvement/improvement_config.json",
-  ],
-}
+```text
+score = 25*D1 + 25*D2 + 25*D4 + 15*D3 + 10*D5
 ```
 
-[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/deep-agent-improvement/SKILL.md:113-138]
+Each dimension is normalized to 0.0-1.0 before weighting. Report a confidence band from k-run variance, fixture count, and contamination lint results. Do not present low-fixture or high-variance runs as definitive.
 
-This key is NEVER included in the prompt. It is stored in the scenario definition file (`benchmark-scenarios/<skill-slug>/scenario-NNN.json`) and loaded only by the scoring pipeline AFTER the run completes. The scoring pipeline compares the captured tool-call trace against this key:
+D1 Routing/Activation:
 
-```javascript
-// Scoring pipeline (post-run):
-const trace = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(runOutputPath, 'utf8'));
-const key = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(scenarioKeyPath, 'utf8'));
+- D1a external advisor selection: advisor top-1/top-2 and confidence threshold.
+- D1b internal smart-router accuracy: expected intent keys and expected resource map.
+- D1c abstention/irrelevance: negatives and near-neighbor skill prompts.
+- D1d utilization conjunction: selected plus internally routed plus first expected resource opened before answer.
 
-// D2: Resource Discovery Score
-const expectedPaths = new Set([
-  ...key.expected_resources,
-  ...key.expected_runtime_assets,
-  ...key.always_resources,
-].map(p => `.opencode/skills/${key.skill_slug}/${p}`));
+D2 Discovery:
 
-const foundPaths = new Set(trace.uniqueFilesRead.filter(p =>
-  p.startsWith(`.opencode/skills/${key.skill_slug}/`)));
+- Expected-resource recall.
+- Irrelevant-load precision.
+- Hit@k and first useful rank.
+- Resource-consumption evidence when available through sentinel/canary, citation, or answer dependency.
+- Hallucinated path penalty.
 
-const hitRate = [...expectedPaths].filter(p => foundPaths.has(p)).length / expectedPaths.size;
-const falsePositiveRate = [...foundPaths].filter(p => !expectedPaths.has(p)).length / (foundPaths.size || 1);
