-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2431:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:20:      - ".opencode/skills/deep-agent-improvement/scripts/dispatch-model.cjs"
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2432:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:37:## ADR-001: Lane Classification of the 16 Scripts
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2433:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:52:Phases 010-012 split references, assets, the agent note, the catalog, and the advisor by lane, but the 16 scripts plus the scorer subtree are still flat at `scripts/`. We need a classification that puts each script under the lane it actually serves, so the tree mirrors the two co-equal lanes.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2434:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:55:- Classification must reflect runtime ownership, not just naming: a script that loop-host spawns on the model-benchmark path may still be shared if both lanes use it.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2435:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:56:- The scorer subtree must move wholesale into model-benchmark so its internal relative requires (`./harness.cjs`, `../lib/cache.cjs`) stay valid.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2436:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:64:**We chose**: Three lane subdirs - agent-improvement (8 scripts), model-benchmark (2 scripts + scorer/), shared (6 scripts).
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2437:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:66:**How it works**: agent-improvement holds score-candidate, generate-profile, rollback-candidate, candidate-lineage, scan-integration, check-mirror-drift, trade-off-detector, benchmark-stability. model-benchmark holds dispatch-model, run-benchmark, and the scorer/ subtree moved as one unit. shared holds loop-host, promote-candidate, materialize-benchmark-fixtures, reduce-state, improvement-journal, mutation-coverage - scripts both lanes invoke or that orchestrate across lanes.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2438:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:77:| Two lanes only, shared folded into agent-improvement | Fewer dirs | loop-host and materialize would be mislabeled as agent-only | 5/10 |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2439:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:80:**Why this one**: A dedicated shared lane is the only honest home for loop-host (which orchestrates both modes) and materialize-benchmark-fixtures (which loop-host spawns on the benchmark path but is fixture infra). It also matches the references/assets layout shipped in 010.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2440:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:99:| materialize misclassified | M | shared is correct: it is fixture infra loop-host spawns, not benchmark-only logic |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2441:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:100:| scorer relative requires break | M | move scorer/ wholesale so internal requires stay valid |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2442:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:112:| 3 | **Sufficient?** | PASS | Three subdirs cover all 16 scripts plus scorer |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2443:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:113:| 4 | **Fits Goal?** | PASS | On the critical path to a fully lane-visible skill |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2444:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:125:- `scripts/agent-improvement/`, `scripts/model-benchmark/`, `scripts/shared/` created via git mv.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2445:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:126:- scorer/ moved into model-benchmark/scorer/ as one unit.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2446:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:135:## ADR-002: TST-1-Preserving Lane Resolution at Spawn Time
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2447:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:149:`loop-host.cjs` is moving to the shared lane, but it spawns children across all three lanes: score-candidate (agent-improvement), materialize-benchmark-fixtures (shared), and run-benchmark (model-benchmark). Its `planInvocation(mode, args)` is a pure planner that returns ordered steps with bare script names, and the TST-1 backward-compat test asserts the default and explicit agent-improvement plans are byte-identical. If lane paths leak into the plan, that identity breaks.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2448:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:161:**How it works**: `planInvocation` continues to emit `{ script: 'score-candidate.cjs', args }` style steps with bare names. A new lane-resolution map in the spawn layer translates each bare name to its `scripts/<lane>/<name>` path right before `spawnSync`. The plan stays byte-identical; only execution knows about lanes.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2449:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:171:| Keep all loop-host children in one lane | No spawn-layer change | Forces a wrong lane on at least two children | 3/10 |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2450:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:181:- Lane knowledge is isolated to the execution boundary.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2451:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:191:| A child spawned at wrong path | H | non-zero exit surfaces loudly; loop-host aborts remaining steps |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2452:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:199:| 1 | **Necessary?** | PASS | loop-host spawns across all three lanes |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2453:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:212:- `loop-host.cjs` runNode/runPlan gain a bare-name to lane-path resolver.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2454:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:215:**How to roll back**: Revert the resolver edit and move loop-host back to the scripts root; the bare `path.join(SCRIPTS_ROOT, name)` then works again at the flat layout.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2455:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:221:## ADR-003: Guarding the dispatch-model Silent-Config-Failure Trap
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2456:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:235:`dispatch-model.cjs` sets `SCRIPTS_ROOT = __dirname` and then resolves `path.join(SCRIPTS_ROOT, '..', 'state')` and `path.join(SCRIPTS_ROOT, '..', 'assets', 'agent-improvement', 'improvement_config.json')`. At the flat layout `..` is the skill root. After moving into `scripts/model-benchmark/`, `..` becomes the scripts root, so both paths miss. `loadConfig` wraps the read in try/catch and returns `{}` on any failure, so a wrong depth produces no error: dispatch silently runs with default model, agent, timeout, and backoff while the journal and dashboard claim the configured values.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2457:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:247:**How it works**: After moving into `scripts/model-benchmark/`, the state and assets joins gain one more `..` (or resolve from a computed skill-root anchor) so they point at the skill root again. A regression test materializes a known `improvement_config.json` and asserts dispatch-model reads the expected `modelBenchmarkConfig` values, catching any future silent fallback to `{}`.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2458:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:288:| 4 | **Fits Goal?** | PASS | protects the model-benchmark lane the move touches |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2459:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:298:- `dispatch-model.cjs` state and assets path joins gain the correct depth.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2460:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/013-scripts-physical-reorg/decision-record.md:301:**How to roll back**: Revert the depth edit and move dispatch-model back to the scripts root, where the original `..` depth is correct.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:2461:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/016-script-subfolder-readmes/description.json:2:  "specFolder": "121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/016-script-subfolder-readmes",
