-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1822:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:116:| `.opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp_server/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts` | Verify/Modify | Confirm the explicit lane maps the new command to the deep-model-benchmark skill |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1823:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:128:| REQ-001 | Lane A behavior is unchanged | Running the agent-improvement lane produces the same workflow as before this phase (behavioral identity); CMD-1 in checklist.md confirms it |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1824:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:129:| REQ-002 | Lane B runs end-to-end from a command | `/deep:start-model-benchmark-loop` (or the lane-asking branch) reaches a benchmark-complete state via `loop-host.cjs --mode=model-benchmark` with no hand-written invocation |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1825:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:130:| REQ-003 | The command asks the use-case lane | `start-agent-improvement-loop.md` asks which lane the user wants and branches additively, with no silent default that hides Lane B |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1826:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:136:| REQ-004 | The advisor routes both lanes | `skill_advisor.py` maps `/deep:start-agent-improvement-loop` to the agent-improvement skill and `/deep:start-model-benchmark-loop` to the model-benchmark skill |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1827:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:137:| REQ-005 | README and gemini mirror present | `.opencode/commands/README.txt` lists the new command and lanes; `.gemini/commands/deep/start-model-benchmark-loop.toml` exists and mirrors the opencode command |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1828:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:146:- **SC-001**: A user can start a model-benchmark run from a command and reach benchmark-complete, while the agent-improvement lane behaves exactly as before.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1829:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:147:- **SC-002**: Both lanes are discoverable: the advisor routes each command to its skill, and the README plus gemini mirror surface the model-benchmark command.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1830:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:157:| Dependency | Model-benchmark runtime contract (phases 003 to 005) | High - no Lane B run without it | Reuse the shipped contract as-is; this phase only wires the command surface |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1831:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:158:| Risk | Lane A regression from the additive branch | Med | Keep lane resolution additive; CMD-1 behavioral identity gate confirms Lane A is unchanged |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1832:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:159:| Risk | Advisor alias already exists but is unverified | Low | REQ-004 verifies routing for both commands against `skill_advisor.py`, not assumed from source presence |
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1833:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:168:- Does the dedicated `/deep:start-model-benchmark-loop` command fully replace the lane-asking branch, or do both stay as parallel entries? (Current design: both stay, the branch routes into the same Lane B workflow.)
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1834:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:177:- **NFR-P01**: The lane-asking branch adds at most one question to the agent-improvement command. It must not add a perceptible startup delay to a Lane A run.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1835:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:180:- **NFR-R01**: Lane A behavioral identity is the reliability invariant. Selecting agent-improvement reproduces the pre-phase Lane A workflow with no observable difference.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1836:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:181:- **NFR-R02**: Lane B reuses the shipped loop-host contract, so a benchmark run is as reliable as the phase 003 to 005 runtime. This phase adds no new failure modes in the runtime.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1837:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:184:- **NFR-S01**: No secrets are introduced into the command, YAMLs, or gemini mirror. Lane B profile and outputs-dir paths stay inside the expected packet-local boundaries.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1838:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:193:- User gives no lane signal: the command asks rather than silently defaulting, so Lane B never gets hidden behind an implicit Lane A choice.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1839:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:194:- Lane B invoked with no `--profile`: loop-host falls back to the default profile (`assets/benchmark-profiles/default.json`), and the YAML must document that default.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1840:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:197:- A Lane B run with `--grader llm` but no reachable executor: the run should surface the dispatch failure rather than silently degrade. The YAML default is `--grader noop` so the happy path is deterministic.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1841:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:198:- The dedicated command is invoked while the advisor source references it but is not recompiled: routing falls back to general handling. REQ-004 verifies routing against `skill_advisor.py`, not source presence.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1842:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:201:- Lane resolution is a one-time branch per invocation. Once a lane is chosen the run stays in that lane, with no mid-run lane switch.
-.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/122-deep-improvement-skill-benchmark-mode/001-skill-benchmark-deep-research/research/gpt55/logs/iter-001.out:1843:.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/121-deep-agent-improvement-benchmark-mode/008-command-lane-asking/spec.md:212:| Risk | 11/25 | The agent-improvement command is a shared live surface; the additive branch must preserve Lane A identity |
